      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: The flow of this function is a little bit hard for me to follow. What if you did something like this?\n```\nbool ppc_vbus_present \u003d false;\nint tcpc_vbus_voltage \u003d 0;\nint tcpc_rv \u003d EC_SUCCESS;\n\n// Invalid argument\nif (level \u003e VBUS_REMOVED)\n  return false;\n\n// Get VBUS, whichever way works\ntcpc_rv \u003d tcpc_get_vbus_voltage(port, \u0026tcpc_vbus_voltage);\n// This check is redundant, but it might save an I2C read\nif (tcpc_rv \u003d\u003d EC_ERROR_NOT_POWERED) {\n  ppc_vbus_present \u003d ppc_is_vbus_present(port);\n}\n\nif (tcpc_rv \u003d\u003d EC_SUCCESS)\n  // Preferred TCPC case\n  switch (level) {\n    // Just check tcpc_vbus_voltage; no need for default\n  }\n} else if (tcpc_rv \u003d\u003d EC_ERROR_NOT_POWERED) {\n  // fallback PPC case\n  // Similar switch to what you have now, but no default\n} else {\n  // TCPC I2C error, if you don\u0027t want to fall back to PPC\n  return false;\n}\n```\nThis is just a little redundant, but I think it makes the thought process more obvious.",
